module

public import TauCeti.Geometry.Manifold.Morse.DG.Circle.Basic
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.DGLocalSystem.Aspherical
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.DGLocalSystem.CellResolution
public import TauCeti.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Eigenvector
public import TauCeti.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Exactness
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Homology.DG.Algebra.KoszulTwist
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Homology.DG.Twisted.Complex

/-!
# DG Morse homology of the circle with coefficients in its loop chains

Let `X` be a pseudo-gradient adapted to the height function `circleCos` of the circle, with its
maximum at `0` and its minimum at `π`, and let `S` be a twisting chain system on its trajectory
spaces. Through a map `θ` from the circle to a space `Y` sending both critical points to `y₀`, the
Barraud–Cornea cocycle of `S` (`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.barraudCorneaCocycle`) has a
single nonzero entry `x = m(0, π)`, a `0`-chain of Moore loops at `y₀`. Take as coefficients the
chain algebra `C_*(Ω_{y₀} Y; R)` itself, a right DG module over itself: the DG local system of the
path fibration of `Y` at `y₀`. The DG Morse complex `C_*(Ω_{y₀} Y; R) ⊗ ⟨0, π⟩` has differential

`D(α ⊗ 0) = dα ⊗ 0 + (-1)^{|α|} α x ⊗ π`,  `D(β ⊗ π) = dβ ⊗ π`

(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.twistedDifferential_circleCosMaxCrit` and
`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.twistedDifferential_circleCosMinCrit`, on the functions from the
critical points to the coefficients, as for `TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.dgMorseComplex`).

This file proves that, when `S` gives the two trajectories from `0` to `π` opposite unit
coefficients `r` and `-r` and `Y` is aspherical with infinite cyclic fundamental group generated by
the image `t` of the loop once around the circle, this complex has the homology of a point: the
augmentation `ε` of the coefficient of `π` vanishes on boundaries
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.loopChainAugmentation_twistedDifferential_circleCos`), takes
the value `1` on the cycle `1 ⊗ π`
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.twistedDifferential_single_circleCosMinCrit_one`), and every
cycle on which it vanishes is a boundary
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos`). For `Y` the circle
itself and `θ` homotopic to the identity, such as the collapse of one of the two arcs between the
critical points, this would give the case `n = 1` of the computation
`H_*(Sⁿ; C_*(ΩSⁿ)) ≅ H_*(pt)` for the path-loop fibration, where the trivial action would give
`H_*(Sⁿ) ⊗ H_*(ΩSⁿ)` (not formalized here: the asphericity, generator and infinite-order
hypotheses are not yet instantiated for `Y = S¹`).

The proof reads the complex in the group ring `R[π₁(Y, y₀)]`. The image of `x` there is
`r g - r t g = g r (1 - t)`, where `g` is the class of the loop traced along the upper half-circle
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.loopChainToGroupAlgebra_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos`,
`TauCeti.fundamentalGroupHom_circleCosHalfLoop_neg_one`); `g` commutes with `t`, which generates.
Over the aspherical `Y`, a cycle of `C_*(Ω_{y₀} Y; R)` is a boundary as soon as its image in the
group ring vanishes
(`TauCeti.exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero`).
So right multiplication by `x` is injective on homology, because `t - 1` is regular for `t` of
infinite order, and every cycle of augmentation zero is a right multiple of `x` up to a boundary,
because the augmentation ideal is generated by `t - 1`. Relabelling the maximum as a cell attached
along `x` to the minimum, the complex is the module of `TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle`, and these are
the two conditions under which it resolves the ground ring
(`TauCeti.exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`), as Brown's
resolution of the circle does with attaching cycle `[γ] - [1]` instead of `x`.

Representing chain systems with coefficients in a ring of characteristic two, such as `ZMod 2`,
give both trajectories the coefficient `1 = -1`
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos_of_forall_eq_one`).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos`: every cycle of the DG
  Morse complex of the cosine with coefficients in the loop chains, of augmentation zero, is a
  boundary.
* `TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.loopChainAugmentation_twistedDifferential_circleCos`: the
  augmentation vanishes on boundaries.
* `TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.twistedDifferential_single_circleCosMinCrit_one`: the cycle
  `1 ⊗ π`, of augmentation `1`.
* `TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos_of_forall_eq_one`: the
  same for coefficients `1` over a ring of characteristic two.

## References

* E. H. Brown, *Twisted tensor products, I*, Ann. of Math. (2) 69 (1959), 223–246, whose
  resolution of the circle the criterion for the homology of a point follows.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Morse homology with differential graded
  coefficients*, Progress in Mathematics 360, Birkhäuser, 2025, Chapters 5 and 7.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Floer homology with DG coefficients.
  Applications to cotangent bundles*, arXiv:2404.07953, §2.
-/

public section

universe u

open Function MonoidAlgebra MulOpposite Set
open scoped Manifold Real Topology

namespace TauCeti

local instance morseDGCircleLoopChainTwoPiPos : Fact (0 < 2 * π) := ⟨Real.two_pi_pos⟩

namespace IsAdaptedPseudoGradient

variable {X : (x : AddCircle (2 * π)) → TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ) x}
  (hX : IsAdaptedPseudoGradient circleCos X) {ι : Type*} {c : ι → ℝ}
  {Y : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Y] {θ : C(AddCircle (2 * π), Y)} {y₀ : Y}
  {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {ind : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos → ℤ}
  (hdense : ∀ x y : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos,
    Ioo (circleCos y) (circleCos x) ⊆ closure (range c))
  (hθ : ∀ x : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos, θ x = y₀)
  (hc : ∀ i (x : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos), c i ≠ circleCos x)
  (S : TwistingChainSystem ind (hX.morseBrokenTrajectorySpaceComp hc) R)

/-! ### The differential -/

section Differential

variable (hind : ind circleCosMinCrit < ind circleCosMaxCrit)
include hind

/-- No entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle of the cosine ends at the maximum. -/
private theorem barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCosMaxCrit (x : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos) :
    (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m x circleCosMaxCrit = 0 := by
  refine (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).one_sided _ _ ?_
  rcases eq_circleCosMaxCrit_or_eq_circleCosMinCrit x with rfl | rfl
  · exact le_rfl
  · exact hind.le

omit hind in
/-- The entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle of the cosine from the minimum to itself vanishes. -/
private theorem barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCosMinCrit_circleCosMinCrit :
    (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMinCrit
      circleCosMinCrit = 0 :=
  (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).one_sided _ _ le_rfl

/-- **The DG Morse differential of the cosine at the maximum.** With coefficients in the loop chain
algebra, the coefficient of the maximum `0` in `D f` is `d (f 0)`: no trajectory ends at the
maximum. -/
theorem twistedDifferential_circleCosMaxCrit (f : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos →
    loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R) :
    twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
        (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
        (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) f circleCosMaxCrit =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R (f circleCosMaxCrit) := by
  rw [twistedDifferential_apply, Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x _ ↦ by
    rw [hX.barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCosMaxCrit hdense hθ hc S hind, op_zero, zero_smul],
    add_zero]

omit hind in
/-- **The DG Morse differential of the cosine at the minimum.** With coefficients in the loop chain
algebra, the coefficient of the minimum `π` in `D f` is `d (f π) + κ (f 0) x`, where `κ` is the
Koszul sign of the degree and `x` is the entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle from the maximum to
the minimum. -/
theorem twistedDifferential_circleCosMinCrit (f : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos →
    loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R) :
    twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
        (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
        (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) f circleCosMinCrit =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R (f circleCosMinCrit) +
        (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
          (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)).koszulTwist 1 (f circleCosMaxCrit) *
          (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMaxCrit
            circleCosMinCrit := by
  rw [twistedDifferential_apply, sum_criticalPoints_circleCos,
    hX.barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCosMinCrit_circleCosMinCrit hdense hθ hc S, op_zero,
    zero_smul, add_zero, op_smul_eq_mul]

/-- The entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle of the cosine from the maximum to the minimum is a
cycle. -/
private theorem cubicalChainDifferential_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos :
    cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R
      ((hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMaxCrit
        circleCosMinCrit) = 0 := by
  rw [(hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).twisting,
    sum_criticalPoints_circleCos, hX.barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCosMaxCrit hdense hθ hc S hind,
    hX.barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCosMinCrit_circleCosMinCrit hdense hθ hc S]
  simp

/-- **The unit at the minimum is a cycle** of the DG Morse complex of the cosine with coefficients
in the loop chain algebra: `D(1 ⊗ π) = 0`. Its augmentation is `1`, so under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos` it generates the
homology. -/
theorem twistedDifferential_single_circleCosMinCrit_one :
    twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
      (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) (Pi.single circleCosMinCrit 1) = 0 := by
  funext y
  rcases eq_circleCosMaxCrit_or_eq_circleCosMinCrit y with rfl | rfl
  · rw [hX.twistedDifferential_circleCosMaxCrit hdense hθ hc S hind,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne circleCosMaxCrit_ne_circleCosMinCrit, map_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
  · rw [hX.twistedDifferential_circleCosMinCrit hdense hθ hc S, Pi.single_eq_same,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne circleCosMaxCrit_ne_circleCosMinCrit, map_zero, zero_mul, add_zero,
      (loopChain_isDGAlgebra Y y₀ R).map_one_eq_zero, Pi.zero_apply]

end Differential

/-! ### The entry from the maximum to the minimum in the group ring -/

section GroupRing

variable {r : R}
  (hS₁ : NormalizedCubicalChain.zeroEquiv _ R (S.chain circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit 0)
    (hX.circleCosTrajectory c 1) = r)
  (hS₂ : NormalizedCubicalChain.zeroEquiv _ R (S.chain circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit 0)
    (hX.circleCosTrajectory c (-1)) = -r)
include hS₁ hS₂

/-- With opposite coefficients `r` and `-r` on the trajectories through the upper and the lower
half-circle, the image of the entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle from the maximum to the minimum
in the group ring is `g r (1 - t)`, where `g` is the class of the loop traced along the upper
half-circle and `t` is the image of the class of the loop once around the circle. -/
private theorem loopChainToGroupAlgebra_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos_eq_single_mul
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
      (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)) = ⊤) :
    loopChainToGroupAlgebra Y y₀ R ((hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
        circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit) =
      single (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom y₀
          (circleCosHalfLoop θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit) (hθ circleCosMinCrit) 1)) r *
        (1 - single (FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
          (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)) 1) := by
  set t := FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
    (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)
  set g := MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom y₀
    (circleCosHalfLoop θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit) (hθ circleCosMinCrit) 1)
  have hgt : g * t = t * g := by
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := Subgroup.mem_zpowers_iff.1 (hgen ▸ Subgroup.mem_top g)
    rw [← hk]
    exact ((Commute.refl t).zpow_left k)
  rw [hX.loopChainToGroupAlgebra_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos_eq_single_add_single hdense hθ hc
    S, hS₁, hS₂,
    fundamentalGroupHom_circleCosHalfLoop_neg_one θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit) (hθ circleCosMinCrit),
    mul_sub, mul_one, single_mul_single, mul_one]
  -- The two sides differ only in the order of `g` and `t`, and in the base point
  -- `0 = ↑circleCosMaxCrit` of `mapOfEq`.
  change single g r + single (t * g) (-r) = single g r - single (g * t) r
  rw [hgt, single_neg, sub_eq_add_neg]

/-- With opposite coefficients on the two trajectories, the entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle
from the maximum to the minimum has augmentation zero. -/
private theorem loopChainAugmentation_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos :
    loopChainAugmentation Y y₀ R ((hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
      circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit) = 0 := by
  rw [← augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra,
    hX.loopChainToGroupAlgebra_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos_eq_single_add_single hdense hθ hc
      S, hS₁, hS₂, map_add,
    MonoidAlgebra.augmentation_single, MonoidAlgebra.augmentation_single, add_neg_cancel]

end GroupRing

/-! ### The homology of a point -/

section Homology

variable (hind : ind circleCosMinCrit < ind circleCosMaxCrit) {r : R}
  (hS₁ : NormalizedCubicalChain.zeroEquiv _ R (S.chain circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit 0)
    (hX.circleCosTrajectory c 1) = r)
  (hS₂ : NormalizedCubicalChain.zeroEquiv _ R (S.chain circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit 0)
    (hX.circleCosTrajectory c (-1)) = -r)

include hS₁ hS₂ in
/-- **The augmentation of the DG Morse complex of the cosine vanishes on boundaries.** With
coefficients in the loop chain algebra and opposite coefficients on the two trajectories from the
maximum to the minimum, the augmentation of the coefficient of the minimum in `D v` is zero. -/
theorem loopChainAugmentation_twistedDifferential_circleCos
    (v : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos → loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R) :
    loopChainAugmentation Y y₀ R
      (twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
        (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
        (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) v circleCosMinCrit) = 0 := by
  have hx := hX.loopChainAugmentation_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hS₁ hS₂
  rw [← augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra] at hx
  rw [hX.twistedDifferential_circleCosMinCrit hdense hθ hc S,
    ← augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra]
  simp only [map_add, map_mul, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_differential, zero_add, hx,
    mul_zero]

variable (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) Y y₀))
  (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
    (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)) = ⊤)
  (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
    (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)))

include hS₁ hS₂ hB hgen hinf in
/-- Right multiplication by the entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle of the cosine from the maximum
to the minimum is injective on homology: a cycle `β` with `β x` a boundary is a boundary. In the
group ring, `β` times the unit `g r` times the regular `1 - t` vanishes, so `β` vanishes there. -/
private theorem exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_eq_mul_circleCos (hr : IsUnit r)
    {β w : loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R} (hβ : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R β = 0)
    (hw : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R w =
      β * (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMaxCrit
        circleCosMinCrit) :
    ∃ γ, cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R γ = β := by
  set t := FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
    (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)
  set g := MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom y₀
    (circleCosHalfLoop θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit) (hθ circleCosMinCrit) 1)
  refine exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB hβ ?_
  have h := congrArg (loopChainToGroupAlgebra Y y₀ R) hw
  rw [loopChainToGroupAlgebra_differential, map_mul,
    hX.loopChainToGroupAlgebra_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos_eq_single_mul hdense hθ hc S hS₁
      hS₂ hgen, ← mul_assoc] at h
  have h' := (isRegular_single_sub_one_of_not_isOfFinOrder hinf).right
    (show loopChainToGroupAlgebra Y y₀ R β * single g r * (single t (1 : R) - 1) =
        0 * (single t (1 : R) - 1) by
      rw [← neg_sub 1 (single t (1 : R)), mul_neg, ← h, neg_zero, zero_mul])
  have hginv : single g r * single g⁻¹ (↑hr.unit⁻¹ : R) = 1 := by
    rw [single_mul_single, mul_inv_cancel, IsUnit.mul_val_inv, one_def]
  simpa [mul_assoc, hginv] using congrArg (· * single g⁻¹ (↑hr.unit⁻¹ : R)) h'

include hind hS₁ hS₂ hB hgen in
/-- Every cycle `α` of the loop chain algebra of augmentation zero is a right multiple `β x` of a
cycle by the entry of the Barraud–Cornea cocycle of the cosine from the maximum to the minimum, up
to a boundary. In the group ring, `α` is a left multiple of `t - 1`, which generates the
augmentation ideal, hence of `x`, whose image is `g r (1 - t)`. -/
private theorem exists_mul_add_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_circleCos (hr : IsUnit r)
    {α : loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R} (hα : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R α = 0)
    (hεα : loopChainAugmentation Y y₀ R α = 0) :
    ∃ β w : loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R, cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R β = 0 ∧
      β * (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMaxCrit
        circleCosMinCrit + cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R w = α := by
  set t := FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
    (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)
  set g := MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom y₀
    (circleCosHalfLoop θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit) (hθ circleCosMinCrit) 1)
  have hker : loopChainToGroupAlgebra Y y₀ R α ∈
      RingHom.ker (MonoidAlgebra.augmentation R (FundamentalGroup Y y₀)) := by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra, hεα]
  rw [MonoidAlgebra.ker_augmentation_eq_span_of_closure_eq_top R (s := {t})
    (by rw [← Subgroup.zpowers_eq_closure, hgen]), Set.image_singleton,
    Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at hker
  obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := hker
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := loopZeroChainToGroupAlgebra_surjective (R := R) (x := y₀)
    (-(h * single g⁻¹ (↑hr.unit⁻¹ : R)))
  have hδ : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R
      (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R 0 e) = 0 :=
    cubicalChainDifferential_lof_zero _ _ _
  -- Subtracting `δ x`, for a zero chain `δ` lifting the multiplier, leaves a cycle with vanishing
  -- image in the group ring, hence a boundary.
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB
    (z := α - cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R 0 e *
      (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMaxCrit
        circleCosMinCrit)
    (by rw [map_sub, hα, IsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.map_mul_eq_zero_of_map_eq_zero
      (loopChain_isDGAlgebra Y y₀ R).toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra hδ
      (hX.cubicalChainDifferential_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hind),
      sub_zero])
    (by
      rw [map_sub, map_mul, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_lof_zero, he,
        hX.loopChainToGroupAlgebra_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos_eq_single_mul hdense hθ hc S
          hS₁ hS₂ hgen, ← hh]
      have hginv : single g⁻¹ (↑hr.unit⁻¹ : R) * single g r = 1 := by
        rw [single_mul_single, inv_mul_cancel, IsUnit.val_inv_mul, one_def]
      have : -(h * single g⁻¹ (↑hr.unit⁻¹ : R)) * (single g r * (1 - single t 1)) =
          -(h * (single g⁻¹ (↑hr.unit⁻¹ : R) * single g r) * (1 - single t 1)) := by
        simp only [neg_mul, mul_assoc]
      rw [this, hginv, mul_one]
      noncomm_ring)
  exact ⟨_, w, hδ, by rw [hw, add_sub_cancel]⟩

include hind hS₁ hS₂ hB hgen hinf in
/-- **The DG Morse complex of the circle with coefficients in the loop chains has the homology of a
point.** Let `θ` send the critical points of the cosine to `y₀`, let `Y` be aspherical at `y₀`
with fundamental group generated by the image `t` of the loop once around the circle, of infinite
order, and let `S` give the two trajectories from the maximum to the minimum opposite unit
coefficients `r` and `-r`. Then every cycle `u` of the DG Morse complex with coefficients in the
chain algebra `C_*(Ω_{y₀} Y; R)` whose coefficient of the minimum has augmentation zero is a
boundary. Since the augmentation vanishes on boundaries
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.loopChainAugmentation_twistedDifferential_circleCos`) and takes
the value `1` on the cycle `1 ⊗ π`
(`TauCeti.IsAdaptedPseudoGradient.twistedDifferential_single_circleCosMinCrit_one`), the homology
is `R`, in the degree of the minimum. -/
theorem exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos (hr : IsUnit r)
    {u : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos → loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R}
    (hu : twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
      (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) u = 0)
    (hε : loopChainAugmentation Y y₀ R (u circleCosMinCrit) = 0) :
    ∃ v, twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
      (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) v = u := by
  have hDmax := hX.twistedDifferential_circleCosMaxCrit hdense hθ hc S hind
  have hDmin := hX.twistedDifferential_circleCosMinCrit hdense hθ hc S
  have hu0 := congrArg (· circleCosMaxCrit) hu
  have hu1 := congrArg (· circleCosMinCrit) hu
  simp only [Pi.zero_apply, hDmax, hDmin] at hu0 hu1
  -- The complex is that of a cell `e₁` (the maximum) attached along `x` to `e₀` (the minimum).
  have hx : (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m circleCosMaxCrit
      circleCosMinCrit ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R
        (-((ind circleCosMaxCrit - ind circleCosMinCrit - 1).toNat : ℤ)) := by
    rw [Int.toNat_of_nonneg (by omega), show -(ind circleCosMaxCrit - ind circleCosMinCrit - 1) =
      ind circleCosMinCrit - ind circleCosMaxCrit + 1 by ring]
    exact (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).mem_graded _ _
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero hx
    (hX.cubicalChainDifferential_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hind)
    (hX.loopChainAugmentation_barraudCorneaCocycle_m_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hS₁ hS₂)
    (fun _ _ hβ hw ↦ hX.exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_eq_mul_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hS₁
      hS₂ hB hgen hinf hr hβ hw)
    (fun _ hα hεα ↦ hX.exists_mul_add_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hind hS₁
      hS₂ hB hgen hr hα hεα)
    (u := Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (u circleCosMinCrit) +
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (u circleCosMaxCrit))
    (by
      refine Finsupp.ext fun i ↦ ?_
      rcases i with ⟨⟨⟩⟩ | ⟨⟨⟩⟩
      · rwa [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.add_apply,
          Finsupp.single_eq_same, Finsupp.single_eq_same, Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne Sum.inl_ne_inr,
          Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne Sum.inr_ne_inl, add_zero, zero_add, Finsupp.coe_zero,
          Pi.zero_apply]
      · rwa [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same,
          Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne Sum.inr_ne_inl, zero_add, Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply])
    (by rwa [loopCellAugmentation_apply, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same,
      Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne Sum.inl_ne_inr, add_zero])
  have hv0 := congrArg (· (Sum.inl ())) hv
  have hv1 := congrArg (· (Sum.inr ())) hv
  simp only [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl, cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr,
    Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same, Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne Sum.inl_ne_inr,
    Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne Sum.inr_ne_inl, add_zero, zero_add] at hv0 hv1
  -- Relabelled back, a preimage of `u` is `v e₁ ⊗ 0 + v e₀ ⊗ π`.
  refine ⟨Pi.single circleCosMaxCrit (v (Sum.inr ())) + Pi.single circleCosMinCrit (v (Sum.inl ())),
    funext fun y ↦ ?_⟩
  rcases eq_circleCosMaxCrit_or_eq_circleCosMinCrit y with rfl | rfl
  · simp only [hDmax, Pi.add_apply, Pi.single_eq_same,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne circleCosMaxCrit_ne_circleCosMinCrit, add_zero, hv1]
  · simp only [hDmin, Pi.add_apply, Pi.single_eq_same,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne circleCosMaxCrit_ne_circleCosMinCrit,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne circleCosMaxCrit_ne_circleCosMinCrit.symm, add_zero, zero_add, hv0]

end Homology

/-! ### Coefficients modulo two -/

include hX in
/-- **The DG Morse complex of the circle with coefficients in the loop chains has the homology of a
point, modulo two.** Over a ring of characteristic two, such as `ZMod 2`, a twisting chain system
which gives both trajectories from the maximum to the minimum the coefficient `1`, as the
fundamental chains of the two-point trajectory space do, gives them opposite unit coefficients,
since `-1 = 1`. So every cycle of the DG Morse complex with coefficients in the loop chain algebra
whose coefficient of the minimum has augmentation zero is a boundary. -/
theorem exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos_of_forall_eq_one [CharP R 2]
    (hind : ind circleCosMinCrit < ind circleCosMaxCrit)
    (hS : ∀ w, NormalizedCubicalChain.zeroEquiv _ R (S.chain circleCosMaxCrit circleCosMinCrit 0) w
      = 1)
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) Y y₀))
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
      (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (FundamentalGroup.mapOfEq θ (hθ circleCosMaxCrit)
      (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom 0 circleCosLoop)))
    {u : criticalPoints 𝓘(ℝ) circleCos → loopChainAlgebra Y y₀ R}
    (hu : twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
      (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) u = 0)
    (hε : loopChainAugmentation Y y₀ R (u circleCosMinCrit) = 0) :
    ∃ v, twistedDifferential (hX.barraudCorneaCocycle isMorse_circleCos hdense hθ hc S).m
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R)
      (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Y y₀) R) v = u :=
  hX.exists_twistedDifferential_eq_circleCos hdense hθ hc S hind (hS _)
    ((hS _).trans CharTwo.neg_one_eq_one.symm) hB hgen hinf isUnit_one hu hε

end IsAdaptedPseudoGradient

end TauCeti
